-- is taken from the pool by key; keep_free (src/store.c) has its forms, mask and declaration kept
-- beside its key all the same (x_checked, store_decl), and when nothing fails NAME is made this
-- machine's label of the key (bound/, written/, the names log), with TEXT its text in the pool. A
-- name a module holds is refused. The object of the names (names_make, names_take) carries a line
-- `t NAMEHEX TEXT` for each name no module holds, so a root says them.
-- src/lang.c (2026-11-22, the same): `--carried`, a count of the names this machine holds now by
-- whether the pool can give their key back (forms, or a declaration), naming those it cannot: what
-- load by key does not reach is measured, not guessed.
-- src/syntax.c (2026-11-22, the same; memory-is-local): the object of the names is a tree, 256 parts
-- by the first byte of the hash of a name (names_line, names_make, names_take), each part an object
-- of its own, so a part no label changed in is shared by the next root and taking reads one part at
-- a time; and it says only names held now (bound/ keeps every name this machine ever checked).
-- src/lang.c, src/syntax.c, src/store.c (2026-11-22, Avik: "Why would I have a single centralized
-- monolith"; "Do it all"): what a root is on two machines. (1) src/lang.c place_first: a machine with
